  "name": "discover-assets",
  "description": "Finds and inspects data assets within Google Cloud. Use for any question that needs to discover data sources or find/inspect schemas, metadata, or domain rules for tables. Relevant when: (1) finding, exploring, or inspecting GCP data assets; (2) retrieving schemas, metadata, or governance policies for a GCP data asset (including a named table); (3) you have a keyword or topic (e.g., \"sales data\") without a table or resource ID; (4) the user asks for enterprise data, metrics, tables, datasets, analytics, business terms, financial reports, or industry statistics (e.g., banking, e-commerce, transit, SEC filings, solar, healthcare) without full table schemas. Don't use for general knowledge questions unrelated to data, or when both explicit table schemas and full SQL are already provided.",
